🔄 How RAG Works

The application follows these steps:

User Question
      │
      ▼
Generate Query Embedding
      │
      ▼
Search Vector Database
      │
      ▼
Retrieve Relevant Documents
      │
      ▼
Build Context
      │
      ▼
Send Context + Question
      │
      ▼
Hugging Face LLM
      │
      ▼
Generate Answer
      │
      ▼
Display Answer

The chatbot retrieves relevant information from the stored documents before generating an answer.

This helps the LLM answer questions based on the application's document collection instead of relying only on its pretrained knowledge.

🐳 Docker Architecture

The project uses a single Docker container to run both the frontend and backend.

                    Docker Container
              ┌──────────────────────────┐
              │                          │
              │   Next.js Frontend       │
              │       :3000              │
              │          │               │
              │          │ /api/*        │
              │          ▼               │
              │   Flask Backend          │
              │       :5000              │
              │          │               │
              │          ▼               │
              │     RAG System           │
              │                          │
              └──────────────────────────┘

The public-facing application uses port 3000.

Next.js forwards API requests such as:

/api/chat

to the Flask backend running internally on:

127.0.0.1:5000
